#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""drive-brief: a short call when he starts driving, only when there is something worth saying (token-free).

  drive-brief tick [--cron]              cron, every minute: a new drive start -> decide within ~1 min -> call or skip
  drive-brief now [--json]               what a drive starting now would get (no call, nothing recorded)
  drive-brief replay [--days 7] [--calendar DIR] [--json]
                                         his recent drives (vault HA drive events): when it would have called and
                                         what it would have said (no calls; --calendar = a calcache dir with those
                                         days, else the live cache; traffic = a proxy: the last leg's minutes vs
                                         Waze's usual minutes)
  drive-brief stats [--days 30] [--json] drives seen, briefings, answered rate, follow-up turns/tools, skip reasons
  drive-brief status [--json]            mode, today's briefings, the current drive
  drive-brief mode off|dry-run|live      kill switch / dry run (logs what it would say) / live (config "mode")

Trigger: `whereabouts ha now` (consumer drive-brief, fresh only) says drive.active under core.drive's rule (the
answer at most DRIVING_MAX_AGE_MIN, 60, min old; `driving`'s), drive.since at most max_start_age_min ago. Drives with a stop shorter than chain_gap_min form one chain: one decision per chain.
Skip: mode off, on a trip abroad (tripclock), night (his local hours night_from..night_to), max_per_day briefings
reached, an outbound call he declined or missed in the last declined_quiet_min (the hub relay's recent calls + the
local call log). Content, most important first (no content -> no call):
  event      the next timed calendar event within event_window_h (no travel leg; one with a train/bus/flight leg
             before it is skipped): Waze minutes from here -> "you'd arrive HH:MM" (likely heading there) or
             "leave by HH:MM"; an event without a town counts only within event_plain_min
  traffic    Waze live - usual >= traffic_min on the likely route: the event's town; office weekday mornings from
             home -> the work town; from the work zone/town in the evening or far from home -> home
  reminders  his own timed reminders due during the drive (Waze minutes, else reminder_window_min)
  parcel     a parcel entry on today's calendar; a parcel-station mail (sender and date only, vault metadata)
             newer than his last stop in that town, when the likely route starts or ends in a parcel.via town
  nav        right after the event line: "Want navigation to <title>?" when that event (with a town, not where he
             is, not the home town) starts within nav_offer_h; his yes makes the relay's navigate tool open Maps on
             his phone to that event's town (place next_event). Only while `phone open --help` works. Config
             nav_offer (default on), nav_offer_h; DRIVE_BRIEF_NAV_OFFER=off
  decisions  Waiting-on-you either/or items (decision-deck): alongside other content, or alone on a drive of
             >= long_drive_min, at most decisions_alone_per_day a day
Spoken text <= max_chars (the relay's cap), lowest priority dropped first. Delivery: `voice-relay call --reason
"drive briefing" --say TEXT` (he can ask follow-ups; the call's fast-lane tools answer). Not answered -> nothing
more. Log ~/.local/state/drive-brief/log.jsonl (decisions, outcomes, follow-up counts from the hub's call log:
counts and tool names only); usage events under bin.drive-brief. Config ~/.config/drive-brief/config.json;
DRIVE_BRIEF=off is the kill switch.
Env (tests): DRIVE_BRIEF_CONFIG, DRIVE_BRIEF_STATE, DRIVE_BRIEF_NOW (ISO), DRIVE_BRIEF_WHERE (command printing the
`vault ha now --json` schema), DRIVE_BRIEF_ROUTES (JSON file {"FROM|TO": {"live": M, "usual": M}}),
DRIVE_BRIEF_CALL_CMD, DRIVE_BRIEF_DECK_CMD, DRIVE_BRIEF_MAIL (JSON file: list of ISO mail dates),
DRIVE_BRIEF_CALLS_CMD (command printing `voice-hub calls --out` JSON, the hub's call log; off = not asked),
DRIVE_BRIEF_REMIND_DIR, DRIVE_BRIEF_HA_EVENTS (JSONL of vault HA events),
DRIVE_BRIEF_TODO_AT (command: TODO.md text at ISO time), DRIVE_BRIEF_NAV_OFFER (off|0 = no nav offer),
DRIVE_BRIEF_PHONE_CMD (the phone CLI), CALCACHE_DIR, ASSISTANT_PROFILE.
Tests: tests/legacy/drive-brief/run.sh in ~/opt/assistant (DRIVE_BRIEF_BIN=/copy).
"""
